# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Env files (never commit secrets)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agent tooling and local skill installs.
# Ignored because the skill trees are sourced in part from SGTechStack/ai-coding-workflow-d2,
# which answers 404 unauthenticated while this repo answers 200 — committing them would
# disclose a private repo into a public one. Same boundary as App-Standards (see wayfinder
# ticket 06). `.claude/skills/*` are additionally absolute symlinks into `.agents/`, which
# would not resolve on any other machine.
.agents/
.claude/
.kiro/
agent/
skills-lock.json

# Build output
target/
node_modules/
dist/
*.log

# Local runtime state, written by running the application locally.
#
# Neither is build output, and `*.log` does not cover either: the log appenders emit `.json`
# (every line is an ECS document -- there is no plain-text appender), and `.data/` is the
# file-based dev H2 database, which is file-based deliberately so that bootstrap idempotence is
# observable across restarts (spec.md S2). Committing it would ship a seeded administrator
# password hash.
.data/
logs/

# Generated documentation
**/javadoc/
**/tsdoc/

# NOTE: `.scratch/` is deliberately NOT ignored on this branch — the wayfinder map and its
# decision tickets are the planning deliverable. This is a conscious departure from the
# `samuelwong` branch, which ignores it.

# Prompt-injection harness output.
#
# `security-tests/test_runner.py` shutil.copytree()s backend/, frontend/ and prd/ into one directory
# PER TEST CASE -- twelve of them -- with no `ignore=` argument, so each copy includes
# frontend/node_modules and backend/target. That is several gigabytes of duplicated build output, and
# none of it is source. `results/` is generated reports.
security-tests/test-submissions/
security-tests/results/
